I now have a complete picture. Here is the full report.

## Overview

The repo at `/home/daniel/sandbox` is **Spring PetClinic REST** rebuilt on **OfficeFloor function injection** (not Spring MVC controllers). Each endpoint is a YAML pipeline of small single-method Java function classes. Build tool is **Maven**. The `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` classes are **generated** (not source files) from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin, so there is no `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse` — those names are only illustrative in `AGENTS.md`.

---

## 1. The POST-owner YAML

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RequireOwnerFields
  next: normalizeTelephone

normalizeTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  next: normalizeEmail

normalizeEmail:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerEmail
  next: rejectDuplicateTelephone

rejectDuplicateTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RejectDuplicateTelephone
  next: rejectDuplicateHousehold

rejectDuplicateHousehold:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RejectDuplicateHousehold
  next: rejectCityAtCapacity

rejectCityAtCapacity:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RejectCityAtCapacity
  next: rejectDailyLimit

rejectDailyLimit:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RejectDailyLimit
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignNamesakeCount

assignNamesakeCount:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignNamesakeCount
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignCustomerCode

