}
```

**RespondWithOwnerCreated.java** — maps to `OwnerDto`, sets bulkSignupWarning, responds 201 with Location header.
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.net.URI;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.OwnerRepository;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerDto;

public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, OwnerRepository ownerRepository,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignup.warning(ownerRepository));
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

### Supporting utilities (same package, referenced by the above)

**AddressNormalizer.java** — trim/collapse/upper-case + expand ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE.
**E164Telephone.java** — E.164 normalization; assumes `+61`, drops single leading `0`, 8–15 digits; `normalize` throws, `normalizeOrNull` returns null.
**BusinessDay.java** — rolls Sat/Sun forward to Monday (note: does NOT skip holidays, unlike the test helper `toBusinessDay`).
**BulkSignup.java** — `warning()` true when > 80 owners already registered today (business day).

(Full contents of these four were read; the load-bearing signatures: `AddressNormalizer.normalize(String)`, `E164Telephone.normalize(String)`/`normalizeOrNull(String)`, `BusinessDay.roll(LocalDate)`, `BulkSignup.warning(OwnerRepository)`.)

---

## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — extends `Person` (which supplies firstName/lastName). Fields with getters/setters: `address` (@NotEmpty), `city` (@NotEmpty), `telephone` (@NotEmpty, @Pattern `^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`), **`email` (`@Column(name="email")`, plain `String getEmail()/setEmail(String)`, no validation/uniqueness constraint)**, `registrationDate` (LocalDate), `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount` (Integer), `householdSize` (Integer), plus `pets` (OneToMany EAGER). The email column is nullable with no unique constraint.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` — interface methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)` (returns null / throws DataRetrievalFailureException)
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

There is **no** `findByEmail` query method — the existing reject functions all scan `findAll()` in memory. There's no email-based lookup, so an email-uniqueness rule would follow that same `findAll()` scan pattern.

---

## 4. Escalation handlers and exception classes

Escalation YAMLs live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`, named `<fully.qualified.ExceptionClass>.yml`, each just mapping to a handler class:

| YAML file | maps to handler |
|---|---|
| `...escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml` | `MissingOwnerFieldsHandler` |
| `...escalation.InvalidEmailException.yml` | `InvalidEmailHandler` |
| `...escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml` | `InvalidTelephoneHandler` |
| `...escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` | `DuplicateTelephoneHandler` |
| `...escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml` | `DuplicateHouseholdHandler` |
| `...escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml` | `CityAtCapacityHandler` |
| `...escalation.DailyLimitExceededException.yml` | `DailyLimitExceededHandler` |
| `...escalation.NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` |

Each YAML content is simply (example, InvalidEmail):
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidEmailHandler
```

Exception + handler classes are in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`. All exceptions are **checked** (`extends Exception`) as required. Representative full contents:

`DuplicateTelephoneException.java` (409 template — the pattern you'd copy for a `DuplicateEmailException`):
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

public class DuplicateTelephoneException extends Exception {
    public DuplicateTelephoneException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
```
`DuplicateTelephoneHandler.java`:
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

import net.officefloor.plugin.section.clazz.Parameter;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;

public class DuplicateTelephoneHandler {
    public void handle(@Parameter DuplicateTelephoneException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<String>> response) {
        response.send(new ResponseEntity<>(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.CONFLICT));
    }
}
```

The other handlers follow the identical shape, differing only in status:
- `InvalidEmailHandler`, `InvalidTelephoneHandler`, `MissingOwnerFieldsHandler` → `HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST` (400). `MissingOwnerFieldsHandler` sends `Map.of("errors", ex.getFields())` instead of a string.
- `DuplicateTelephoneHandler`, `DuplicateHouseholdHandler`, `CityAtCapacityHandler` → `CONFLICT` (409).
- `DailyLimitExceededHandler` → `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429).
- `NotFoundExceptionHandler` → `ResponseEntity.notFound().build()` (404, empty body).

`NotFoundException.java` — this is the repo's analogue of the `OwnerNotFoundException` mentioned in the task:
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

public class NotFoundException extends Exception {
