## 6. Tests and how to run them

Test sources under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

- **`AcceptanceTest.java`** — the only concrete test currently. It contains one test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail()` which is directly about creating owners with duplicate emails: creates an owner with `uniqueEmail()`, then POSTs a second owner reusing that email and **expects HTTP 409 Conflict**. (Full contents below.)
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.status;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** email-unique: Reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner. Respo... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsDuplicateEmail() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		a.put("email", uniqueEmail());
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("email", a.get("email").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}
}
```
Important implication: this test currently would **fail** against the code as-is, because `NormalizeOwnerEmail` only validates syntax and there is no duplicate-email reject function in the `owners.POST.yml` pipeline. Implementing "email-unique" means adding a reject step (e.g. `RejectDuplicateEmail` returning 409 via a new `DuplicateEmailException`/handler) into the pipeline, mirroring `RejectDuplicateTelephone`.

- **`AcceptanceBase.java`** — abstract base (full contents read above). `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`. Provides helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid owner), `createOwner()/createOwnerOk()`, `getOwner()/fetchOwner()`, `deleteOwner()`, `uniqueEmail()` = `"owner"+seq+"@example.test"`, `fillCity()`, `createMany()`, pinned reference tables (CITY_REGION, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS for 2026), and `toBusinessDay()` (which also skips holidays). Uses Jackson 3 `tools.jackson.databind`.

- **`AuditLogCapture.java`** — test utility capturing the `AUDIT` logger (Logback ListAppender) so audit side-effects can be asserted.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/resources/application.properties` — test config (not printed).

**Build tool: Maven.** There is a wrapper `./mvnw`. Run tests with:
```
./mvnw test
```
(or `./mvnw verify` / `./mvnw -Dtest=AcceptanceTest test` for the single class). Note `mvn test` triggers `generate-sources` first, which regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` from `openapi.yml` (openapi-generator + build-helper add `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` as a source root). So any DTO field change must be made in `openapi.yml`, not in Java.

