### Key takeaways for editing to add an email-uniqueness rule
- Add a new function class (e.g. `RejectDuplicateEmail`) in `.../rest/function/owner/`, scanning `ownerRepository.findAll()` comparing lower-cased emails, mirroring `RejectDuplicateTelephone`.
- Add a checked `DuplicateEmailException extends Exception` and a `DuplicateEmailHandler` (409) in `.../rest/escalation/`, plus the escalation YAML `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateEmailException.yml`.
- Wire the new step into `owners.POST.yml` (e.g. after `normalizeEmail`, before or alongside `rejectDuplicateTelephone`), since email is normalized to lower-case in `NormalizeOwnerEmail` before any duplicate check.
- The email is optional, so the reject step must skip when the incoming email is null/blank.
